da3-41cc-890f-412611dc9ea0","oracle_text":"Flash\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\nWhen Ty Lee enters, tap up to one target creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as you control Ty Lee.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-11-21","toughness":"1","type_line":"Legendary Creature — Human Performer Ally"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wind Drake","oracle_id":"d6ffdaf0-ac08-4de9-bbce-2eab2f86bcca","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-09-30","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Drake"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Ty Lee, Chi Blocker ceases to be under your control before its ability resolves, you will still tap the targeted creature, but it will untap normally during its controller's next untap step.","oracle_id":"081ad4e3-cda3-41cc-890f-412611dc9ea0","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Ty Lee, Chi Blocker leaves the battlefield, you no longer control her, and her effect ends.","oracle_id":"081ad4e3-cda3-41cc-890f-412611dc9ea0","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another player gains control of Ty Lee, Chi Blocker, her effect ends. Regaining control of Ty Lee, Chi Blocker won't cause the effect to resume.","oracle_id":"081ad4e3-cda3-41cc-890f-412611dc9ea0","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
